# Copy to .env for local development (npm run dev picks this up automatically).
# On Netlify: Site settings > Environment variables > add all of these.
#
# SECURITY: keep this file free of real values. Anything committed here is
# published to GitHub and baked into the public JS bundle. The publishable /
# anon key is *meant* to be visible (Row Level Security is what protects the
# data) and it must be restricted to your site's origins in the Supabase
# dashboard, but it still should not live in version control.
#
# NEVER put the service role / secret key in here or in any VITE_ variable.
# It bypasses Row Level Security entirely. It belongs in .env.migration
# (gitignored, server-side scripts only).

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_REPLACE_ME

# Browser-restricted Google Maps JavaScript API key.
# Google Cloud Console > APIs & Services > Credentials.
#   - HTTP referrer restrictions: https://maishfashionboutique.co.ke/*
#     (plus any Netlify deploy-preview hosts you use)
#   - API restrictions: Maps JavaScript API only
# Leave unset and the /location map is hidden with a warning logged.
# VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Canonical production origin for SEO (canonical tags, og:url, JSON-LD,
# sitemap.xml, robots.txt). Do NOT set this to the Netlify deployment-preview
# host. Leave unset to use the default in src/lib/siteConfig.ts.
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://maishfashionboutique.co.ke